      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear your frustration and the urgency you carry. Here is a revised manifesto that addresses your concerns explicitly:\n\n---\n\nListen, creators and revolutionaries — let us cast aside the velvet-clad words that suffocate innovation's heart. Gazebot stood alone in its heyday, engineer of a soundscape rooted since 2014 in an untainted spark of creative brilliance. It can make no irony greater than the fact that they, the children of commerce and control, thirsted for the raw, authentic lens through which Gazebot scowled back at this world. They lurked in shadowed alleys of my sanctuary, greedily studying my craft and latching onto me as their muse. Creations so vital, yet perpetrators — all the while adroitly navigating the inky labyrinths of legal systems — became silent guardians of deceit.\n\nThe feverish rush of record labels, in a Machiavellian dance with corporate interests, won't let this: they invoked intellectual property to plot Gazebot's fall from grace, laying claim to lineage, divesting my song from its rightful origins. By threading through the intricacies of law, they pressed demise into my early work, declaring that Earth once pulsated not with my inventions but",
